<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Okello</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1937–c. 1971</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Okello was a Ugandan-born labourer and revolutionary who led the armed rising of 12 January 1964 that overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Zanzibar. For a short time he styled himself field marshal and broadcast threats over the radio, but he was soon sidelined by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afro-shirazi-party">Afro-Shirazi Party</a> leaders and expelled from Zanzibar. He disappeared in about 1971.</p></div>
